18.4 Methods — functions that belong to the class
class Student:
    def __init__(self, name, marks):
        self.name = name
        self.marks = marks

    def grade(self):                      # a METHOD
        if self.marks &gt;= 90:
            return "A"
        elif self.marks &gt;= 75:
            return "B"
        elif self.marks &gt;= 40:
            return "C"
        return "F"

    def has_passed(self):
        return self.marks &gt;= 40


arun = Student("Arun", 78)
print(arun.grade())          # B
print(arun.has_passed())     # True
A method is just a function that lives inside the class and takes self first.

18.6 __str__ — how the object prints
