14.1 But for 2-D, a plain loop gives you rows, not values
b = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])

for row in b:
    print(row)         # [1 2] then [3 4]   -&gt; ROWS, not numbers
To reach the individual values you need a nested loop, or np.nditer:
for row in b:
    for value in row:
        print(value)         # 1 2 3 4

for value in np.nditer(b):   # the NumPy way, any number of dimensions
